abstract:
The simplest algorithm in machine learning, and the one that teaches the most. KNN has no training phase, no parameters and no assumptions — it just remembers the data and takes a vote. We cover the distance metrics, why scaling is mandatory rather than advisable, how k trades bias against variance, why the curse of dimensionality destroys it, and how KD-trees and Ball trees make prediction tractable.}
